{
  "id": "light_beam_path_for_a_prism",
  "title": "Light Beam Path for a Prism",
  "description": "The light beam dispersion rainbow color effect of a prism. When white light shines on a prism surface it is broken down to different color components based on wavelength and refractive index variations.",
  "type": "chart",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Light Beam Path for a Prism\n\nThe [refractive index](refractive-index-d_1264.html \"Light refractive index\") for light at the interface between two media varies with the wavelength of the light. \n\n- **Blue light**: wavelength λ between 420 and 490 nm\n- **Red light**: wavelength between 650 to 750 nm\n\nWhen white light shines on a prism surface it is broken down to different color components."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "wavelength",
          "label": "Wavelength (nm)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 550,
          "unit": "nm"
        },
        {
          "id": "incident_angle",
          "label": "Incident Angle (degrees)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 45,
          "unit": "degrees"
        },
        {
          "id": "prism_angle",
          "label": "Prism Apex Angle (degrees)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 60,
          "unit": "degrees"
        },
        {
          "id": "refractive_index",
          "label": "Refractive Index",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1.52,
          "unit": ""
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "refraction_angle",
          "label": "Refraction Angle",
          "formula": "Math.asin(Math.sin(inputs.incident_angle * Math.PI / 180) / inputs.refractive_index) * 180 / Math.PI",
          "unit": "degrees",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "deviation_angle",
          "label": "Deviation Angle",
          "formula": "inputs.incident_angle + Math.asin(inputs.refractive_index * Math.sin((inputs.prism_angle * Math.PI / 180) - Math.asin(Math.sin(inputs.incident_angle * Math.PI / 180) / inputs.refractive_index))) * 180 / Math.PI - inputs.prism_angle",
          "unit": "degrees",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chart",
      "headers": [
        "Color",
        "Wavelength (nm)",
        "Refractive Index"
      ],
